<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mulambwa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1830</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Mulambwa Santulu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mulambwa was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litunga">Litunga</a> (king) of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Lozi</a> kingdom of Barotseland from about 1780 to about 1830, one of its longest reigns. He reformed the kingdom's laws and strengthened royal authority over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> floodplain. His death was followed by a succession war that weakened the Lozi and helped the Kololo under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sebetwane">Sebitwane</a> to conquer them around 1840.</p></div>
